,"id":441937681,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MTkzNzY4MQ==","user":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-05-25T20:24:14Z","updated_at":"2018-11-27T06:09:55Z","body":"**Michael Bayer ([@zzzeek](https://github.com/zzzeek)) wrote:**\n\nFlatten operator precedence for comparison operators\n\nThe operator precedence for all comparison operators such as LIKE, IS,\nIN, MATCH, equals, greater than, less than, etc. has all been merged\ninto one level, so that expressions which make use of these against\neach other will produce parentheses between them.   This suits the\nstated operator precedence of databases like Oracle, MySQL and others\nwhich place all of these operators as equal precedence, as well as\nPostgresql as of 9.5 which has also flattened its operator precendence.\n\nCo-authored-by: Mike Bayer <mike_mp@zzzcomputing.com>\nFixes: #3999\nChange-Id: I3f3d5124a64af0d376361cdf15a97e2e703be56f\nPull-request: https://github.com/zzzeek/sqlalchemy/pull/367\n\n\n→ f8a3f14e4f86\n","author_association"